//! Health, measurement, session, and semantic tools.

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const FIND_DUPLICATES: &str = "Deterministic Type-1, Type-2, and Type-3 clone families. Files named .gen. or .generated., and files whose header says they were generated by openapi-generator.tech, are boilerplate unless include_boilerplate is set. include_declarative defaults to true (high recall); false suppresses data-only catalogs and still keeps model, schema, and contract clones. include_strings also compares multi-line string payloads such as inline SQL. min_similarity is 0 to 1 as a fraction, or above 1 through 100 as a percentage. min_tokens, mode, top_n, include_tests, and include_classified bound the families. This is a structural clone review, and it does not delete code.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const FIND_DEAD_CODE: &str = "Conservative unreferenced-symbol review queue. Go main.go and func main are entry points. Exported symbols stay at confidence 50 and are omitted when min_confidence is higher. Confidence tiers: 25 is a whole unreferenced file, 50 is an exported symbol nothing reaches, 85 is a private symbol nothing references. Bounded static analysis never reaches 100. Each candidate is id, label, kind, language, and span. A type-only import does not keep its target live. path and kinds narrow the queue. top_n caps it. include_tests and include_classified add those nodes. A candidate is a review item, and it is not a proof that deleting it is safe.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const RUN_AUDIT: &str = "Repository structure and evidence-completeness audit. Cycles are production file-level runtime dependencies. They are not containment edges and not type-only imports. category collects only that section. min_severity and max_findings bound the findings. At least 200 parsed edges with resolved edges under one fifth of that is REVIEW. Pass include_capabilities for the build capability matrix. include_tests defaults to true and attaches revision-bound external test evidence when you pass test_evidence (an inline weavatrix.test-evidence.v1 object) or test_evidence_path (a repository-relative file of that schema). The two evidence arguments are mutually exclusive. The engine does not execute the suite. base_ref, changed_files, and debt scope the audit to a change. include_classified adds hidden nodes. A scoped call is the usable size; an unscoped call on a large tree is the full census.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const COVERAGE_MAP: &str = "Hang an existing LCOV, Istanbul, Tarpaulin, or LLVM report onto graph nodes. The engine does not run tests and does not invent a percentage. It opens the first of lcov.info, coverage/lcov.info, .weavatrix/coverage/lcov.info, tarpaulin-report.json, target/tarpaulin/tarpaulin-report.json, target/llvm-cov/coverage.json, and coverage/coverage-final.json. measured_coverage.present true means a report was parsed. present false with a complete status is unmeasured, and it is not 0% and not a pass. source says Weavatrix did not execute tests. path limits the map to one file. top_n caps the rows. Weavatrix Quality writes .weavatrix/coverage/lcov.info; any other producer of those filenames works the same way.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const HOT_PATH_REVIEW: &str = "Rank functions by static complexity times resolved call fan-in. score = complexity_cost x (1 + resolved call fan-in), where complexity_cost = extent lines + 3 x cyclomatic + 10 x loop nesting. min_score is a floor on that score. cyclomatic_threshold, call_threshold, and loop_depth_threshold drop functions below those floors. path limits the ranking to one file. top_n caps the rows. include_tests and include_classified add those nodes. This uses the graph. It does not read a profiler. Use perf_attribution when you have a measurement table.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const PERF_ATTRIBUTION: &str = "Correlate a measurement table you already wrote with the declarations that changed between those revisions. measurements_file is a repository-relative tab- or comma-separated file and is required. Comment rows starting with # are ignored. Rows without a finite metric are reported as skipped. metric is the numeric column name, for example nanoseconds per operation, and is required. The engine measures nothing itself. A missing file is a read error (the operating system reports the missing path). It is not an empty attribution. revision_column defaults to commit; unresolvable revisions are skipped. min_delta_percent marks steps inside the noise band as flat. max_revisions walks the most recent rows (default 12); each distinct revision costs one analysis of that revision. direction, top_n, path, include_tests, and include_classified bound the blamed declarations.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const REBUILD_GRAPH: &str = "Rebuild the derived in-memory graph for the active repository and store that state back on the session lane. No source file is written. The answer is the node and edge counts before and after. Call graph_stats for the census, the evidence split, and freshness. mode, precision, and scope select how the rebuild is bounded. A child repository argument reads that child and does not move the process pin.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const OPEN_REPO: &str = "Retarget this process to another local repository. path is required. The call is refused unless the process was started with --allow-retarget. Without that flag the launch root stays fixed, and a child graph is requested with the repository argument on the tool you actually want. build, mode, and precision apply only after a retarget is allowed. Graphs unused for 20 minutes unload. Do not use this to escape a pin, and do not use git_fetch as a substitute for a checkout you already have.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const LIST_KNOWN_REPOS: &str = "List the graphs this process has open and the recent request log. recent_requests rows carry agent, repository, tool, time, reused, and ok. requests_total counts completed calls. The agent value comes from the agent argument on each call, truncated to about 80 characters; omitted calls are stored as unset. There is no separate request id. This is the session log. It is not a scan of every repository on disk.";

pub(in crate::operations::catalog) const SEMANTIC_LINK: &str = "Rank symbols for a text query with the deterministic local token hash weavatrix-token-hash-v1. The hash scores the symbol name, the path, up to 12 nearby doc-comment lines, the declaration line, and up to 24 body lines. Test paths rank lower. The model is local and lexical. A neural embedding is a different input: pass a non-empty vectors array of objects with node (a graph id) and values (numbers) to link caller-supplied vectors instead. An empty vectors array without query is an error and builds no links. Omit query only in that vectors mode. model, min_similarity, top_k, and selection bound the ranking.";
